From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Sat, 27 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: keep the SRAM fast path for jumbo-ingress
 offloaded flows

LAN-bound offloaded flows are staged in the PSE SRAM
(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_FAST_PATH), a buffer shared by all ports, so a download
that saturates a LAN port ends in PSE admission drops while the deep hw
forwarding DRAM buffer stays unused. Staging every LAN-bound flow in
DRAM is not possible either: the DRAM buffer holds at most 2048 bytes of
payload per descriptor (HWFWD_PAYLOAD_SIZE_2K is the hardware maximum,
the 2-bit payload size field only selects 2K/1K/512/256), so a bridged
flow between two jumbo-MTU LAN hosts would lose its first large segment
in the hw forwarding stage and wedge.

Choose the staging location per flow instead: resolve the ingress
net_device from the flow rule's META key and keep AIROHA_FOE_IB2_FAST_PATH
(PSE SRAM, payloads chained in pages, any frame size) when the ingress
MTU allows frames above the 2048 byte DRAM slot; clear it otherwise,
so standard-MTU ingress (e.g. the WAN downlink) gets the deep DRAM
queue. If the ingress device cannot be resolved, default to the SRAM
path, which is safe for any frame size.

The hw entries the flowtables install (IPv4 HNAPT, IPv6 5T) do not
carry the ingress port, so the entry of a bridged flow also serves the
same tuple when it later arrives on another port of the bridge (a
station moving between wifi and a wired port, or an L2 device in the
middle). Judging such a flow by its first ingress alone would leave a
jumbo port behind a DRAM-staged entry. Bridge ports and bridge masters
are therefore judged by every lower device of the bridge: with any
jumbo port in the bridge, bridged flows from its standard-MTU ports to a
LAN GDM take the SRAM path too.

The ingress lookup lives in its own helper so that it does not add
locals next to the flow rule parsing in airoha_ppe_flow_offload_replace().
A rule without a redirect action has no egress device; the helper does
not touch it then. The comment above the FAST_PATH selection described
the old unconditional behaviour and is dropped.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -348,7 +348,8 @@ static int airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare(
 					struct airoha_foe_entry *hwe,
 					struct net_device *netdev, int type,
 					struct airoha_flow_data *data,
-					int l4proto, u8 dsfield)
+					int l4proto, u8 dsfield,
+					bool ingress_jumbo)
 {
 	u32 qdata = FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_SHAPER_ID, 0x7f), ports_pad, val;
 	int wlan_etype = -EINVAL, dsa_port = airoha_get_dsa_port(&netdev);
@@ -411,10 +412,7 @@ static int airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare(
 			val |= FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_PSE_PORT, pse_port) |
 			       FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_DSCP, dsfield) |
 			       AIROHA_FOE_IB2_PSE_QOS;
-			/* For downlink traffic consume SRAM memory for hw
-			 * forwarding descriptors queue.
-			 */
-			if (airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev))
+			if (airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev) && ingress_jumbo)
 				val |= AIROHA_FOE_IB2_FAST_PATH;
 			if (dsa_port >= 0)
 				val |= FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_FOE_IB2_NBQ,
@@ -1092,6 +1090,47 @@ static int airoha_ppe_entry_idle_time(st
 	return airoha_ppe_get_entry_idle_time(ppe, e->data.ib1);
 }
 
+static bool airoha_ppe_dev_is_jumbo(const struct net_device *dev)
+{
+	return READ_ONCE(dev->mtu) + ETH_HLEN + 2 * VLAN_HLEN + ETH_FCS_LEN >
+	       AIROHA_MAX_PACKET_SIZE;
+}
+
+static int airoha_ppe_lower_dev_is_jumbo(struct net_device *dev,
+					 struct netdev_nested_priv *priv)
+{
+	return airoha_ppe_dev_is_jumbo(dev);
+}
+
+static bool airoha_ppe_flow_ingress_is_jumbo(struct flow_rule *rule,
+					     struct net_device *odev)
+{
+	struct net_device *idev, *br = NULL;
+	struct flow_match_meta meta;
+	bool jumbo = true;
+
+	if (!odev)
+		return jumbo;
+
+	flow_rule_match_meta(rule, &meta);
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	idev = dev_get_by_index_rcu(dev_net(odev), meta.key->ingress_ifindex);
+	if (idev && netif_is_bridge_port(idev))
+		br = netdev_master_upper_dev_get_rcu(idev);
+	else if (idev && netif_is_bridge_master(idev))
+		br = idev;
+
+	if (br)
+		jumbo = airoha_ppe_dev_is_jumbo(br) ||
+			netdev_walk_all_lower_dev_rcu(br,
+					airoha_ppe_lower_dev_is_jumbo, NULL);
+	else if (idev)
+		jumbo = airoha_ppe_dev_is_jumbo(idev);
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
+	return jumbo;
+}
+
 static int airoha_ppe_flow_offload_replace(struct airoha_eth *eth,
 					   struct flow_cls_offload *f)
 {
@@ -1104,6 +1143,7 @@ static int airoha_ppe_flow_offload_repla
 	u8 dsfield = 0, l4proto = 0;
 	int err, i, offload_type;
 	u16 addr_type = 0;
+	bool ingress_jumbo;
 
 	if (rhashtable_lookup(&eth->flow_table, &f->cookie,
 			      airoha_flow_table_params))
@@ -1204,8 +1244,10 @@ static int airoha_ppe_flow_offload_repla
 	    !is_valid_ether_addr(data.eth.h_dest))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	ingress_jumbo = airoha_ppe_flow_ingress_is_jumbo(rule, odev);
 	err = airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare(eth, &hwe, odev, offload_type,
-					   &data, l4proto, dsfield);
+					   &data, l4proto, dsfield,
+					   ingress_jumbo);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
